.TH ACC-TUI 1 2026-10-22 "ACC" "ACC Manual"
.SH NAME
acc-tui \- terminal UI for observing and driving ACC collectives
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B acc-tui
.RB [ \-\-profile
.RB { operator | user }]
.RB [ \-\-resume
.RI [ session_id ]]
.br
.B acc-tui
.B \-\-list\-sessions
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B acc-tui
is the operator's terminal UI for one or more ACC collectives.
It subscribes to \fBacc.\fR\fIcollective_id\fR\fB.>\fR on the NATS bus for
every collective it observes, and presents the collective as a strip of
screens: Soma (the dashboard), Nucleus, Prompt, Board, Compliance, Memory,
Performance, Comms, Ecosystem, Marketplace, Catalogs, Configuration and
Diagnostics.
.PP
Most operators start it through
.BR acc (1),
which first checks that a collective answers and settles the session's
workspace.
.B acc-tui
itself attaches without either check and keeps retrying the bus with
backoff.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-profile " {" operator | user }
Which screens sit on the strip and where the TUI starts.
\fBoperator\fR shows everything and starts on Soma (the default);
\fBuser\fR shows Prompt and Compliance and starts on Prompt, with the
rest one Ctrl+A chord away.
.TP
.BR \-\-resume " [" \fIsession_id\fR ]
Resume a saved Prompt session; without a value, the latest.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-sessions
List saved sessions, newest first, and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B ?
Help for the current screen.
.TP
.B Ctrl+A
The navigation leader: Ctrl+A followed by a key moves to another screen.
.TP
.B Ctrl+P
The command palette: jump to any screen or run any action of the current one.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ACC_NATS_URL
The bus (default \fBnats://localhost:4222\fR).
.TP
.B ACC_COLLECTIVE_IDS
Comma-separated collectives to observe, for example \fBsol\-01,sol\-02\fR.
.TP
.B ACC_COLLECTIVE_ID
A single collective, used when \fBACC_COLLECTIVE_IDS\fR is unset.
.TP
.B ACC_TUI_PROFILE
The same as \fB\-\-profile\fR.
.TP
.B ACC_SESSIONS_DIR
Where Prompt sessions are saved (default \fI~/.acc/sessions\fR).
.TP
.B ACC_TUI_LOG_DIR
Where \fIacc\-tui.log\fR is written (default \fI/app/logs\fR, falling back
to \fI./acc\-tui\-logs\fR when that is not writable).
Logs never go to the terminal: they would draw over the screen.
.TP
.B ACC_TUI_WEB_PORT
Serve the web bridge on this port (0 or unset disables it).
.TP
.B ACC_ROLES_ROOT
The roles tree; otherwise found through the layout in
.BR acc (1).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.acc/sessions
Saved Prompt sessions.
.TP
.I $ACC_TUI_LOG_DIR/acc\-tui.log
The TUI log, rotated at 5 MB with three backups.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR acc (1),
.BR acc-cli (1),
.BR acc-webgui (1),
.BR acc-deploy (1)
